# Shine Metals — frontend environment
#
# Copy to .env for local development. Everything here is compiled into the
# bundle and served to every visitor, so nothing secret belongs in this file
# — that is what VITE_ means, not a suggestion.
#
# Both variables are optional. The app builds and runs with neither.


# ── Where the API is ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave this blank for the website. In a browser the app and the API share
# an origin, so a relative /api works and Vite proxies it in development.
#
# It exists for the Android shell: there the page is served from
# https://localhost, where /api is the shell itself rather than the server,
# so the app build needs an absolute URL. `npm run build:app` sets it.
VITE_API_URL=


# ── Address autocomplete ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WattleAddr, on the supplier and consignee address fields. Free tier is
# 5,000 lookups a month.
#
#   1. Sign up at https://wattleaddr.com.au
#   2. Create a PUBLISHABLE key (waddr_pk_…) in the console
#   3. Lock it to your domains — shinemotorinvoice.vercel.app and localhost
#
# Publishable keys are meant to be in the browser; they only work from the
# domains listed in the console. Never put a secret key here.
#
# Left blank, the address field falls back to OpenStreetMap through the
# API — which needs no key at all — and below that to an ordinary text box.
# The yard must be able to write a docket with a third-party service
# unreachable, out of quota, or not set up yet.
#
# NOTE: a waddr_sk_test_… key was once committed here and pushed to the
# public repository. Revoke it in the WattleAddr console before using this.
VITE_WATTLEADDR_KEY=
